  "unit": "Unit 3 - Manipulating & Solving Equations",
  "description": "Comprehensive lesson covering Unit 3 - Manipulating & Solving Equations for SAT Math preparation.",
  "duration": 45,
  "content": "<p><strong>Unit 3 - Manipulating & Solving Equations — Title &amp; Goal</strong><br />Comprehensive lesson covering Unit 3 - Manipulating & Solving Equations for SAT Math preparation.</p>\n\n\n<h3>Key idea</h3>\n<p>Read the idea and scan the rules. Focus on how the symbols behave.</p>\n<p>A <strong>linear equation</strong> has the general form:</p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></math>\n<h3>Next idea</h3>\n<p>Build on the previous idea. Notice what changes and what stays the same.</p>\n<p><strong>Steps:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Move variable terms to one side.</li>\n<li>Move constants to the other.</li>\n<li>Divide by the coefficient of <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></math>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>\n<p><strong>SAT Tip:</strong> Always combine like terms before solving.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>\n<p>Multiply through by the least common multiple (LCM) of the denominators:</p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>6</mn><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>⇒</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></math>\n<hr />\n<p>A <strong>quadratic equation</strong> has the form:</p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>\n<h3>Next idea</h3>\n<p>Build on the previous idea. Notice what changes and what stays the same.</p>\n<p><strong>Methods:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Factoring</strong> (when easy integers exist)<br/>\n   Example:  </li>\n</ol>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>\n<ol start=\"2\">\n<li><strong>Quadratic Formula</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>±</mi><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>\n<ol start=\"3\">\n<li><strong>Completing the Square</strong><br/>\n   Turn <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> into <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math> form.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<p>Definition:  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mtext> </mtext><mtext>or</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></math>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mtext>or</mtext><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mtext>or</mtext><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>\n<p><strong>SAT Tip:</strong> Always check for extraneous solutions in absolute value and radical equations.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Equations with square roots:</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>\n<ol>\n<li>Square both sides:</li>\n</ol>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>\n<ol start=\"2\">\n<li>Expand:</li>\n</ol>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>\n<ol start=\"3\">\n<li>Rearrange:</li>\n</ol>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>\n<ol start=\"4\">\n<li>Factor:</li>\n</ol>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mtext>or</mtext><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>\n<ol start=\"5\">\n<li><strong>Check:</strong> Plug into original equation - <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> gives <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> (false), so only <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> works.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<p>Two main methods on the SAT:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Substitution</strong></p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Solve one equation for one variable, substitute into the other.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Elimination</strong></p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Add/subtract equations to eliminate one variable.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">{</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></math>\n<p>Add both:</p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>\n<p>Substitute into <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></math>:</p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>\n<hr />\n<p>1) Solve: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>17</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n2) Solve: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n3) Solve: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n4) Solve: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n5) Solve: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n6) Solve:</p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">{</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></math>\n<hr />\n<p>1) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n2) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n3) LCM is 12: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n4) Factors of 20 that sum to -9: (-5, -4) → <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> → <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n5) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math> or <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math><br/>\n6) Add: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>, then <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math></p>\n\n<h3>Quick practice</h3>\n<p>Try these on your own. Check your steps, not just the final answer.</p>\n1) Solve: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>17</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n<br />\n1) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n\n2) Solve: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n<br />\n2) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n\n3) Solve: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n<br />\n3) LCM is 12: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n\n<h3>Mixed practice set</h3>\n<p>These mix everything above. Time yourself and reflect on any mistakes.</p>\n\n4) Solve: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n<br />\n4) Factors of 20 that sum to -9: (-5, -4) → <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> → <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n\n5) Solve: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n<br />\n5) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math> or <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math><br/>\n\n6) Solve:\n<br />\n6) Add: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>, then <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>",
